# The Cessna 182S Skylane's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/c182.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The 182S's undercarriage is fixed, so nothing here names the gear. Its
# propeller is not fixed-pitch, and the lever has items of its own. The engine
# is fuel-injected, so there is no carburettor heat to pull; the cowl flaps,
# which the flight model has not got, are the pilot's to confirm.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, and the propeller area called clear
confirm Seats upright, belts and harnesses fastened, both doors latched
confirm Fuel selector on both tanks, master switch and beacon on
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller lever fully forward
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle open a quarter of an inch

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running and idling evenly
confirm Cowl flaps open for the ground run
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up until the take-off is briefed
confirm Brakes tried as the aeroplane first moves
confirm Compass and the turn coordinator watched round the turns
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 20.5 Flaps up, or twenty degrees off a short field
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator trim set for take-off
confirm Controls free and correct, and the gauges read across as power comes up
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2300.0 2450.0 Full throttle, the governor holding 2,400 rpm
check velocities/vc-kts >= 57.0 Ease the nose wheel off at 57 knots

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up once the aeroplane is climbing away
range velocities/vc-kts 76.0 94.0 Climb at 80 to 90 knots
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich below 3,000 feet
confirm Cowl flaps open, and the temperatures and pressures in the green

phase cruise
range fcs/advance-cmd-norm 0.80 1.00 Propeller set between 2,100 and 2,400 rpm
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.55 0.95 Power set between 55 and 80 per cent
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned for the cruising height
confirm Cowl flaps closed, altimeter set, and the aeroplane trimmed to hold its height

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.10 0.65 Power back for the descent
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture enriched as the aeroplane comes down
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up until the speed is back in the white arc
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure, and its weather noted
confirm Cowl flaps as the cylinder temperatures ask, cabin heat and air as wanted

phase approach
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller fully forward, ready for a go-around
range velocities/vc-kts 62.0 80.0 Approach at 65 to 75 knots
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 38.5 Flaps as the approach asks, up to the full thirty-eight degrees
confirm Landing light on, the runway in sight and the circuit clear

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 20.0 38.5 Flaps twenty degrees to full
range velocities/vc-kts 58.0 72.0 Over the fence at 60 to 70 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle closed in the flare
confirm Touch down on the main wheels with the nose wheel held well off
confirm Hold the nose up as the speed falls, and brake only once it is down

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back to a taxi power
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller lever fully forward again
confirm Cowl flaps open, landing light off, and the trim reset
